# Milestone: M5
# Covers: cross-spec composition: event subscriber writes to a slot that has
#         a slot-change watcher; chain: e! → slot write → slot-change sub fires.
#         Tests that event-driven slot writes trigger downstream slot-change
#         watchers (spec cross-spec §2.1 chaining rule).
#
# blocked: at(cond) body event chain gap; Event.new()+Object.new() available but chain broken
# matrix-row: reactive-event
#
# Reason:
#   Requires both Event.new() (T59) and Object.new() (T69) stdlib bindings,
#   plus scratch-frame body dispatch for both the event subscriber body (which
#   writes obj.x) and the slot-change subscriber body.  The chain correctness
#   (event emit → slot write → slot-change subscriber) is a composition of
#   urbi_event_emit_async + OP_SETSLOT + urbi_emit_slot_change_if_subscribed.
#
# Activate when both stdlib bindings + body dispatch are wired.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at T59 + T69 + M5-scratch-frame):
#   var e = Event.new();
#   var obj = Object.new();
#   var chain_fired = 0;
#   at (e?) obj.x = 1;
#   at (obj.x.changed?) Realm.chain_fired = Realm.chain_fired + 1;
#   e!;
#   chain_fired
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000000] nil
#   [00000001] nil
#   [00000002] 0
#   [00000003] nil
#   [00000004] nil
#   [00000005] nil
#   [00000006] 1
